"FRAMING (parameterized flagging): the transient mhp/mep component is not a special case — it is a dirty flag that CARRIES a parameter. A plain dirty flag is the zero-payload case ('recompute me'); the mhp transient is 'recompute the hp delta, applying this mhp'. The applier system consumes it exactly like a flag and additionally reads its payload; being per-tick transient, it self-clears like any flag latch. This unifies the two ecs features (auto dirty flags + per-tick transient components) as one concept: parameterized flags. Possible future generalization (not required for this epic): let the entity/ecs macro declare a flag with a typed payload directly, instead of a bespoke transient component + hand-written applier per case."